    {
      "id": "claim_319925f9c50b49af8b82e966d1d77488",
      "statement": "beginOrQueue registers a message atomically under one lock: either it joins the active run's queue (started=false) or the caller takes ownership of a fresh run (started=true), which closes the window where a message could be appended to a queue nobody drains. A new run is refused with errTooManyRuns once the user has maxRuns active runs, and maxRuns <= 0 disables the cap.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/server/turns.go#L452-L485",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:caeee124417ae40b9c762c3fbd7db06f81682bce00768f3d5acaf84e55de04a5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9d7562997ab345cdb0997abbf1c6d1f8",
      "statement": "turnQueue keeps two ordered slices, pending follow-ups and steers consumed at the next round boundary; each queuedMsg carries an id, text, Held flag, timestamp and attachments so a queued or steered follow-up can carry files through a reorder and the drain.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/server/turns.go#L21-L48",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b19db8887c8ee28cc5c591c200c8a76be05183c6179c468e53ca3ab83b01cc12:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
